 skip="Adding lots of fiber fast? Go slowly, drink water.",
 caption="Comment GUT for Sun Yoon's 7-Day Fiber Ladder.\nBlueberries in water float. That's the whole trick. Eat them instead: 1 cup ≈ 3.6 g fiber (USDA). In a Lancet 2019 review of large studies, people eating 25–29 g fiber a day tended to have longer lives and less heart disease (observational). Frozen is fine.\nGo up slowly and drink water.",
